{
  "id": "explore-time-series-display-options",
  "title": "Compare display options",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Explore panels that differ in one display option to see what interpolation, fill opacity, and stacking change."
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "compare-interpolation",
      "title": "Line interpolation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "navigate",
          "reftarget": "/d/000000016/time-series-graphs?from=now-1h&to=now&timezone=browser&dtab=More-Examples",
          "content": "Open **Time series graphs** on its **More Examples** tab."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-589']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Find **Linear** in the **Interpolation** row."
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "Straight lines join the points."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-590']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Focus on **Smooth**."
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "Curves join the points instead. The curves don't add measurements between them."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-591']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Focus on **Step before**."
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "The line is drawn as steps between points. It stays level, then jumps straight up or down to the next value."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "compare-fill",
      "title": "Fill opacity",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-573']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Focus on **Lines** again. Its fill opacity is 0, so there is no shading under the line."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-586']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Focus on **Fill opacity = 10**. A faint shade sits under the line."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-testid='data-testid Tab Time Series Introduction']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "content": "Select the **Time Series Introduction** tab."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-1']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Focus on **Simple graph**."
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "With fill opacity set higher, at 40, the area under each line is shaded heavily. Fill opacity changes only how transparent or solid that shading is. It doesn't change the values the line shows."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "compare-stacking",
      "title": "Stack series",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-1']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Focus on **Simple graph** again. Its **Stack series** option is **Off**."
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "Hover over the graph. The tooltip shows each series' own value, and each line's height is that value, counted up from zero."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-3']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/000000016",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true,
          "content": "Focus on **Stacked lines**. Its **Stack series** option is **Normal**."
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "Hover over this graph. Each series is drawn on top of the one below it, so the top line shows their total, not the top series' own value.\n\nBe cautious with stacking. Only the bottom series starts from zero. Each line above it starts where the one below ends, so a line can rise because the series under it grew, not because its own value did."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
